from pathlib import Path
for country in ['uk','au']:
 au=country=='au'; name='Australia' if au else 'United Kingdom'; symbol='AU$' if au else '£'; demo='/?region='+country
 head=f'''<!doctype html><html lang="{'en-AU' if au else 'en-GB'}" data-region="{country}"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><meta name="robots" content="noindex,nofollow,noarchive"><title>ron. — A startup proposal for wealth advisers / {name}</title><meta name="description" content="A startup proposal for wealth advisory firms: client control, professional review and less administration. Explore the fictional adviser and client demo."><link rel="icon" href="/mark.svg"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/landing/landing.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/landing/proposal.css"><script>try{{document.documentElement.dataset.theme=localStorage.getItem('ron-appearance')==='dark'?'dark':'light'}}catch{{}}</script></head><body><div class="proposal-notice">STARTUP PROPOSAL · FICTIONAL DEMO · {name.upper()}</div><header><a class="logo" href="/{country}/" aria-label="Ron proposal home">ron<span>.</span></a><div class="nav-actions"><a href="/{country}/partners/">For founding firms</a><div class="region"><a href="/uk/" {'aria-current="page"' if not au else ''}>UK</a><span>/</span><a href="/au/" {'aria-current="page"' if au else ''}>AU</a></div><button class="theme" id="theme" aria-label="Switch colour theme">◐</button></div></header>'''
 footer=f'''<footer class="wrap proposal-footer"><span class="logo">ron<span>.</span></span><p>A concept for adviser-led private wealth software. No advice, accounting, legal or execution service is currently offered by this demo. Proposed service providers would need the relevant authorisations. Illustrative data and calculations only.</p><div><a href="{demo}#rules">Rules, sources & coverage →</a><a href="{demo}#tour">Adviser feature tour →</a></div></footer><script src="/landing/proposal.js"></script></body></html>'''
 regulation='appropriate AFS licence authorisations or authorised-representative arrangements, registered financial advisers and TPB-registered tax agents' if au else 'appropriate FCA permissions and qualified tax accountancy, AML supervision and professional registrations'
 localrules='Australian resident investing, company tax, conditional CGT discounts, franking, super caps and ATO/ASIC obligations' if au else 'UK personal and company investing, ISA/EIS conditions, dividend and gains treatment, pensions and HMRC/Companies House obligations'
 body=f'''<main><section class="hero proposal-hero"><img class="hero-art" src="/landing/canoe.svg" alt="" aria-hidden="true"><div class="wrap"><p class="proposal-eyebrow">FOR FIRMS THAT WANT TO BUILD SOMETHING BETTER</p><h1>A startup for<br>wealth advisers.</h1><p class="hero-lead">More control for hands-on clients.<br>Less paperwork for the people looking after them.</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="button" href="{demo}#tour">Take the 5-minute tour <span>↗</span></a></div><p class="admission-note">A proposal to explore with founding advisory firms.</p></div></section>
<section class="wrap proposal-section"><h2>The idea.</h2><div><p class="proposal-lead">A client says, “I want to invest in this.” Your firm gets the whole picture.</p><p>What they own personally and through companies. Where the money could come from. What needs selling. Their available limits, the tax now and later, and what they want the investment to do.</p><p>They can test a plan themselves. You review the recommendation, call them with the context in front of you, and record what you agreed. Once they sign the approved version, connected systems could carry out the authorised steps.</p><p>AI would handle document classification, proposed data extraction and follow-up questions. Your professionals keep responsibility for advice, tax work and approvals.</p></div></section>
<section class="wrap proposal-section"><h2>The adviser’s desk.</h2><div><p>Every client’s portfolio, requests, documents and filing questions in one place. Their number beside the plan. Previous conversations and notes on the right.</p><div class="desk-preview"><div><span>CLIENT REQUEST</span><h3>Alex wants to invest {symbol}200,000.</h3><p>Compare ownership and funding. Review tax assumptions. Ask about the preference shares.</p><a href="{demo}#adviser">Open the adviser workspace →</a></div><aside><strong>Alex Morgan</strong><small>Client contact · sample</small><span>Call client ↗</span><hr><strong>Last conversation</strong><p>Keep two years of spending accessible. Review the startup offer before committing.</p></aside></div><p>The aim is to help a small firm serve more clients while keeping the relationship personal. The demo shows the workflow; capacity savings still need validating with a real firm.</p></div></section>
<section class="wrap proposal-section"><h2>What would it do?</h2><div class="proposal-steps"><article><span>01</span><div><h3>Read the paperwork.</h3><p>Documents and emails become proposed investment records, dates and questions. Grants, employee shares, contracts, statements and travel evidence stay attached.</p></div></article><article><span>02</span><div><h3>Compare the plan.</h3><p>Personal, company or split ownership. Growth, distributions, reinvestment, disposal and extraction. Show the source accounts, quantities and projected holdings changes.</p></div></article><article><span>03</span><div><h3>Approve the instructions.</h3><p>Professional review, client signature and a versioned execution plan. Sell, settle, reserve tax, transfer and invest in order. A failure stops later steps.</p></div></article><article><span>04</span><div><h3>Finish the filing.</h3><p>Checklists grouped by submission date and person or company. Known information is pre-filled. Clients answer what’s missing and confirm the final numbers.</p></div></article></div></section>
<section class="wrap proposal-section"><h2>Follow the journey.</h2><div><p>Start with the customer: connect accounts, check limits, propose an investment, approve the reviewed plan and finish the filing. Then follow the firm: verify records, review the request, call the client and oversee the authorised steps.</p><p><a href="{demo}#journey/customer">The customer journey →</a></p><p><a href="{demo}#journey/firm">The firm’s workflow →</a></p><p><a href="{demo}#limits">Try the tax-headroom and bank-protection checks →</a></p></div></section>
<section class="wrap proposal-section"><h2>Who would buy it?</h2><div><h3>The firm.</h3><p>A regulated wealth advisory business with tax accountancy in-house, complex clients and an administrative bottleneck. The firm onboards its own clients and reviews advice before it reaches them.</p><h3>The client.</h3><p>A founder after an exit, business owner or executive who wants to stay hands-on. They have investments across personal accounts, companies, {'super' if au else 'pensions'} and employee shares, and want professionals checking the decisions.</p><div class="proposal-hypothesis"><strong>Initial customer hypothesis</strong><p>{symbol}5m–25m investable portfolios, excluding the primary home. A proposed {symbol}2m entry threshold. These are discovery assumptions, not evidence of demand.</p></div><p>Clients get a simple view. Their adviser gets the detail and controls. Home equity counts towards wealth but is never proposed as investment funding.</p></div></section>
<section class="wrap proposal-section"><h2>The business case.</h2><div><p class="proposal-lead">Proposed platform fee: £10,000 per client office, per year.</p><p>Shareholder accounts included. Advice, accounting, legal work and filing fees would be agreed separately. This is a pricing hypothesis, not a current service offer. {'The fee is denominated in GBP; Australian billing, conversion and taxes need commercial validation.' if au else 'The platform fee alone is 0.5% of a £2m portfolio or 0.2% of a £5m portfolio, before professional fees.'}</p><table class="market-table"><thead><tr><th>Adoption scenario</th><th>Client offices</th><th>Annual platform revenue</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>100 firms × 20 clients</td><td>2,000</td><td>£20m</td></tr><tr><td>250 firms × 40 clients</td><td>10,000</td><td>£100m</td></tr><tr><td>500 firms × 100 clients</td><td>50,000</td><td>£500m</td></tr></tbody></table><p class="proposal-small">These are arithmetic adoption scenarios across the proposed UK/Australia market, not a measured TAM, forecast, customer count or valuation. A credible TAM needs the number of qualifying households, suitable firms and willingness to pay.</p><p class="proposal-small">The FCA’s 2026 UK wealth report covers 500 investment-management firms and over 5.5m retail clients; typical advised portfolios are around £650k, below the proposed entry threshold. Those clients cannot all be counted as this product’s market. Australian qualifying demand remains to be measured. <a href="https://www.fca.org.uk/data/wealth-management-survey-report-2026" target="_blank" rel="noopener">FCA source ↗</a></p></div></section>
<section class="wrap proposal-section"><h2>Built around your firm.</h2><div><p>The proposed platform works alongside existing accounting and tax systems. Xero could handle bookkeeping and expenses; ron would add the investment, planning, documents and approvals layer.</p><p>The {name} demo covers {localrules}. <a href="{demo}#rules">See the source-dated rule register and known changes →</a></p><p>Advice remains with the authorised firm. Tax work remains with its registered professionals. Legal work goes to appointed lawyers. For {name}, eligibility would require {regulation}.</p><a class="button" href="/{country}/partners/">The founding-firm proposal <span>↗</span></a></div></section>
<section class="wrap proposal-section proposal-last"><h2>Would your clients<br>want this?</h2><div><p>How many clients want more control, with your team checking the plan? Where does your team spend time that software should handle? What would need to be connected before you trusted it?</p><p>This is a working proposal for firms that could build and operate the business. The next step is to test it with real advisers and clients.</p><a class="button" href="{demo}#tour">Explore the proposal in the demo <span>↗</span></a></div></section></main>'''
 Path(f'dist/{country}/index.html').write_text(head+body+footer)
 partners=f'''<main class="wrap founding-page"><p class="proposal-eyebrow">FOUNDING ADVISORY FIRMS / {name.upper()}</p><h1>Help shape the firm<br>you want to run.</h1><p class="proposal-lead">A software startup proposal for advisers who want to give hands-on clients more control and reduce the work around each decision.</p><a class="button" href="{demo}&mode=adviser#adviser">Explore the adviser workspace <span>↗</span></a><section class="proposal-section"><h2>What your team gets.</h2><div><ul><li>A consolidated view of each client’s holdings, loans, liquidity and objectives.</li><li>A queue of investment requests with source records, assumptions, tax comparisons and open questions attached.</li><li>Contact details and previous interactions beside the review.</li><li>AI-assisted document intake, with extracted fields awaiting professional checks.</li><li>Versioned client instructions, signed authorisation and dependent execution steps.</li><li>Dated filing checklists, pre-filled figures and explicit questions.</li></ul><p>All of these are demonstrated with fictional data. AI, providers and filings are not connected.</p></div></section><section class="proposal-section"><h2>What the firm controls.</h2><div><p>Review every recommendation and tax adjustment before showing it to the client. Approve or reject the route. Onboard your own clients. Decide which portfolios, providers and service scope you support.</p><p>A client can explore scenarios and request a review. A scenario is not released professional advice. Material changes to an approved plan require a fresh review and signature. Execution must verify funding, account permissions, limits and confirmed provider results.</p></div></section><section class="proposal-section"><h2>Who could operate it?</h2><div><p>A firm with wealth advice and tax accountancy in-house and {regulation}. Legal work needs qualified lawyers where required. Registrations and permissions must be checked for the actual services and clients.</p><p>Being a software proposal does not remove advice, tax-agent, client-money, privacy or execution obligations. Operating arrangements would need professional design before launch.</p></div></section><section class="proposal-section"><h2>Validate the economics.</h2><div><p>The working price is £10,000 annually per client office, with professional fees separate. This needs testing against client value, staff time, provider costs and support requirements.</p><p>Use a small cohort to measure document handling, time per review, filing corrections, completion rates and the client experience. No proven efficiency gain or revenue uplift is claimed.</p></div></section><section class="proposal-section"><h2>The questions to answer.</h2><div><ol><li>Which existing clients would ask for this?</li><li>What would make it worth the proposed price?</li><li>Which providers and accounting systems must connect first?</li><li>Which steps would the firm trust the system to prepare or execute?</li><li>Would your firm want to build and operate it?</li></ol><a class="button" href="{demo}#tour">Take the guided feature tour <span>↗</span></a></div></section></main>'''
 Path(f'dist/{country}/partners/index.html').write_text(head+partners+footer)
